  "reason": "The records collectively make the later strategy plausibly reconstructible. R1, R3, R12, and R18 directly establish mechanical alloying followed by SPS as a route from fine or BCC HEA powders to dense, hard bulk alloys, while R2 and R19 further establish SPS densification and temperature-dependent phase precipitation in compositionally related Al-, Ti-, V-, Fe-, and Co-containing systems. R1, R4, R12, and R19 show that oxygen introduced during powder processing or SPS can form dispersed oxide phases in a BCC matrix, including TiO, alumina, and mixed oxides, rather than merely being incidental contamination. R6 and R7 connect Al-, Ti-, and Cr-containing protective oxide scales, including spinels and Al-rich inner oxides, with improved oxidation resistance through restricted diffusion, and R16 supplies the related concept of a protective surface layer acting as a barrier in a chloride-containing environment. Thus an expert could plausibly propose high-temperature SPS of ball-milled MgAlTiVFeCo powder to maximize density and generate oxide barrier phases that support passivation and oxidation resistance. The exact 1000 °C optimum, the specific AlV2O4/FeAl2O4/FeTiO3 assemblage, the loc"
